('guide-hoppers-comparison','guide','hoppers-vs-string-hoppers','Hoppers vs string hoppers: what is the difference?','Comparison','Hoppers are bowl-shaped pancakes with a crisp edge, while string hoppers are steamed nests of rice noodles. Both are served with savoury accompaniments. Choose a hopper for a crisp texture or string hoppers for a soft base that absorbs curry.','Despite their similar English names, these are different preparations. A hopper is cooked in a pan, and egg hoppers include an egg in the centre. String hoppers are pressed into thin strands and steamed.\n\nFor breakfast or dinner, ask what accompaniments the kitchen offers. Coconut sambol and curry can complement either dish. Ingredients and availability vary by venue. If you have dietary restrictions, confirm them directly with the kitchen.',ARRAY['appa vs indi appa','hoppers versus string hoppers','breakfast comparison']::TEXT[],ARRAY['Hoppers: bowl-shaped, pan-cooked pancake; crisp rim and soft centre.','String hoppers: steamed rice-flour noodle nests; soft texture.','Serving: both can be paired with savoury curries and sambol.']::TEXT[],ARRAY['hoppers','string-hoppers']::TEXT[],'https://www.srilanka.travel/culinary-tourism/food-range.php','Sri Lanka Tourism — Food',TRUE,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
('guide-breakfast-ideas','guide','sri-lankan-breakfast-ideas','Three Sri Lankan breakfast ideas to try','Meal ideas','Try egg hoppers with sambol, string hoppers with coconut gravy and curry, or coconut roti with a savoury relish. Each offers a different texture and flavour. Ask the kitchen about spice levels and ingredients, or adapt the accompaniments to your own preferences at home.','For a crispy breakfast, start with an egg hopper and choose a relish you enjoy. For a softer meal, pair string hoppers with kiri hodi and a curry. Coconut roti offers a more compact option, with a savoury accompaniment on the side.\n\nThese are meal suggestions, not fixed recipes or nutritional claims. Try a different combination on your next visit or explore our dish guides to learn the preparation behind each choice.',ARRAY['breakfast ideas','what to eat for breakfast','Sri Lankan morning meals']::TEXT[],ARRAY['Egg hopper with a savoury sambol.','String hoppers with kiri hodi and curry.','Coconut roti with a relish.']::TEXT[],ARRAY['hoppers','string-hoppers']::TEXT[],'https://exploresrilanka.lk/a-real-taste-of-sri-lanka-the-traditional-sri-lankan-breakfast/','Explore Sri Lanka — Traditional breakfast',TRUE,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
